  "id": "boxa601",
  "title": "Chapter 43: Planning in India",
  "order": 43,
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "g3skv4g",
      "content": "Economic planning refers to the systematic use of resources by the government to achieve specific economic and social objectives. In India, economic planning was introduced to promote rapid economic growth, reduce poverty, increase employment and achieve balanced regional development."
    },
    {
      "type": "statStrip",
      "stats": [
        {
          "label": "Planning Commission",
          "value": "1950",
          "icon": "calendar"
        },
        {
