        }
      ],
      "id": "tutzskh"
    },
    {
      "id": "y7megms",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Meaning of Economic Planning"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Economic planning in India initially relied on Five-Year Plans formulated by the Planning Commission.",
        "The Planning Commission was set up in March 1950 as an advisory body to formulate national development strategy.",
        "India executed a total of 12 Five-Year Plans alongside several Annual Plans between 1951 and 2017.",
        "NITI Aayog (National Institution for Transforming India) replaced the Planning Commission in 2015.",
        "NITI Aayog operates as a policy think-tank emphasizing cooperative federalism and a bottom-up approach."
      ],
      "id": "6hn4akm"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "8iewfwk",
      "content": "• Economic planning is the process through which the government decides how resources will be used."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "6jzdio2",
      "content": "• It involves setting targets and policies for economic development."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "y68zo08",
      "content": "• It aims to achieve balanced growth and social welfare."
    },
    {
      "id": "td10aqk",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "2. Objectives of Economic Planning in India"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "fymo7t7",
      "content": "• Economic growth and development."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "9cgosnh",
      "content": "• Reduction of poverty and unemployment."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "x5djcze",
      "content": "• Modernization of economy."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "kqdh8q9",
      "content": "• Self-reliance and economic independence."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "alc2ukl",
      "content": "• Balanced regional development."
    },
    {
      "id": "vrkdttn",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "3. Planning Commission"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "nakvsdd",
      "content": "The Planning Commission was established in 1950 to formulate Five-Year Plans for India's economic development. It worked under the chairmanship of the Prime Minister."
    },
    {
      "id": "r0l1cvg",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Functions of Planning Commission"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "2iwrdk3",
      "content": "• Formulate Five-Year Plans."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "fos7ibk",
      "content": "• Assess resources of the country."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "glvl52o",
      "content": "• Determine priorities for development."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "hdq0ww0",
      "content": "• Monitor implementation of plans."
    },
    {
